           ╔══════════════════════ The Fruity CSS engine — 1 · Inheritance  (1/10) ══════════════════════╗
           ║                                                                                             ║
           ║  CSS styles CONTROLS the same way it styles HTML elements: by a #id (unique) or a .class    ║
           ║  (shared). The first big idea is INHERITANCE — set a property once on a container and       ║
           ║  everything inside picks it up, so you never repeat yourself. Below, ONLY the outer box     ║
           ║  names a colour; the text box and label inside simply inherit it.                           ║
           ║                                                                                             ║
           ║ The CSS                                        The bash — how it's built                    ║
           ║ ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐   ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐ ║
           ║ │/* the app stylesheet — authored once, lik│   │ft_stylesheet name=demo style="$DEMO_CSS" │ ║
           ║ │#inhbox { color: crimson; }   /* the conta│   │ft-div name=inhbox                    # th│ ║
           ║ │#spec   { }                   /* the box n│   │    ft-textfield name=spec value=…    # #s│ ║
           ║ │                                          │   │end_ft_div                                │ ║
           ║ │                                          │   │# ── the dropdown changes the PARENT, live│ ║
           ║ │                                          │   │ft-modify inhbox color=dodgerblue     #  ▸│ ║
           ║ └━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━─────────────────┘   └━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━──────────────────┘ ║
           ║                                                                                             ║
